  "content": {
    "title": "Masters reveals start time for 2026 Honorary Starters ceremony",
    "text": "Updated April 7, 2026, 1:02 p.m. ETThe 2026 Masters will begin with the Honorary Starters Ceremony at 7:25 a.m. on Thursday.Golf legends Jack Nicklaus, Gary Player, and Tom Watson will serve as this year's honorary starters.The tradition of an honorary first shot dates back to 1941 with amateur Francis Ouimet.The official role of Honorary Starter began in 1963 with Jock Hutchison and Fred McLeod.AUGUSTA, Ga. — The 2026 Masters won't officially begin until Thursday's Honorary Starters Ceremony, and we now know when that will begin.Jack Nicklaus, Gary Player and Tom Watson will kick off this year's 90th Masters at Augusta National Golf Club with the opening tee shots. The three legends at the Masters, with 11 green jackets between them, will officially begin the tournaments by hitting driver down the first hole.The ceremony is scheduled to begin at 7:25 a.m. on the No. 1 tee.When did Honorary Starter ceremony begin?Having someone hit the first shot at the Masters dates to 1941, when amateur Francis Ouimet played the first round before withdrawing. While the role of Honorary Starter wasn’t official quite yet, Ouimet’s appearance at the urging of Tournament co-founder Bobby Jones was enough to plant the seed of an idea that would eventually start the tradition, per the Masters website.Who has been a Masters Honorary Starter?Jock Hutchison: 1963 – 1973Fred McLeod: 1963 – 1976Byron Nelson: 1981 – 2001 (non-consecutive)Gene Sarazen: 1981 – 1999Ken Venturi: 1983Sam Snead: 1984 – 2002Arnold Palmer: 2007 – 2016Jack Nicklaus: 2010 – presentGary Player: 2012 – presentLee Elder: 2021Tom Watson: 2022 – present",
